# Every endpoint except /health needs an Entra ID access token for THIS API
# (role: Recruiter or HiringManager). With the Azure CLI signed in as a user who has a role:
#   az account get-access-token --scope <scope> --query accessToken -o tsv
# where <scope> is api_scopes.candidate from: terraform -chdir=infra/identity output api_scopes
# Tokens last about an hour.
@token = paste-token-here
@host = http://localhost:5101

### Create a candidate
POST {{host}}/candidates
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada@example.com"
}

### List all candidates
GET {{host}}/candidates
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Search candidates by name
GET {{host}}/candidates?search=ada
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get a candidate by id (replace the id)
GET {{host}}/candidates/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update a candidate (replace the id)
PUT {{host}}/candidates/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ada King",
  "email": "ada@example.com"
}

### Health check
GET {{host}}/health
